course: dictionary
lesson: 3356
title: Except: leaving things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Except» means not including, or leaving something out. In «Everyone except Tom went to the park», the word except takes Tom out of the group, so Tom did not go.
explain: Look at the words before and after except. «Open every day except Sunday» means the shop is open on all the other days, because Sunday is left out. Check by swapping in your meaning: "open every day, not including Sunday" makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «Except» can also mean but, or apart from the fact that. «I'd come, except that I'm ill» means I would like to come, but I am ill. Be careful not to mix it up with «accept», which sounds the same but means to take what is offered.
fact: Except means not including, or leaving out.
fact: «Except» often comes after words like every, all, or everyone.
fact: «Except for» and «except that» are useful phrases: «except that» means but, or apart from the fact that.
fact: «Except» and «accept» sound alike but mean different things: accept means to take what is offered.
fact: Frogs live on every continent except Antarctica, and they come in amazing shapes and sizes.
exercise: «Everyone except Tom went to the park.» Did Tom go to the park? | *No, he did not go | Yes, he went with everyone | Yes, he went after everyone else | Yes, he went first
exercise: «I'd come, except that I'm ill.» What does except that mean here? | a list of everything | every single day | *but, apart from the fact that | to take what is offered
exercise: «There are about 250 kinds of owl, and they live on every continent except Antarctica.» Which continent is left out? | Europe | Asia | Africa | *Antarctica
test: «Open every day except Sunday.» Is the shop open on Sunday? | Yes, it is open all week | *No, Sunday is left out | Open on Monday only | Only open on Sunday
test: Which word means to take what is offered? | expect | except | *accept | excite
exam: «There are over 2,000 kinds of rodent, living on every continent except Antarctica.» What does except tell you here? | It adds more places to the list | *It leaves out Antarctica, where rodents are not found | It means to take what is offered | It means but, apart from the fact that
